{"work_id":"tirumbippaar","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":22,"scene_status":"verified","unit_count":6,"units":[{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s022-u001","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s022-d001","speaker_label":"பாமா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":30,"printed_page":22}]},"translation":{"english_text":"How many days can we stay in a hotel? Find a house quickly."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s022-u002","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s022-d002","speaker_label":"பரந்தாமன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":30,"printed_page":22}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Let the house-hunting wait.... Come, at least today let's go around and see the city."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s022-u003","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s022-d003","speaker_label":"பாமா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":30,"printed_page":22}]},"translation":{"english_text":"Uh-uh...first we must start our family life."}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s022-u004","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s022-d004","speaker_label":"பரந்தாமன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":30,"printed_page":22}]},"translation":{"english_text":"We will. Why are you in such a hurry? What has starting a family got to do with seeing Chennai?"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s022-u005","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s022-d005","speaker_label":"பாமா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":30,"printed_page":22}]},"translation":{"english_text":"What is there in Chennai?"}},{"id":"tirumbippaar-en-s022-u006","kind":"dialogue","status":"verified","source":{"source_record_id":"tirumbippaar-s022-d006","speaker_label":"பரந்தாமன்","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":30,"printed_page":22}]},"translation":{"english_text":"What is there in Chennai? They tell story after story about Kannagi Salai. They say the lighthouse gleams in the sun. Eyes that have not seen the zoo and Marina beach are sinful eyes, they say. Hmm...come! Queen of my love, ornamental divine form of the mansion of beauty, picture that even nectar could not paint. Come, let's go. (They leave.)"}}]}